\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A virtual laboratory is a software environment for scientific computation. Interoperability requires compatible data, model, and execution interfaces so computations can be transferred or combined.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
This is a software and research-infrastructure direction, not a supplied mathematical conjecture.

Source-record limitation: The supplied assessment flags software interoperability as a broad design question rather than a mathematical conjecture.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Develop interoperable virtual laboratories that combine simulation methods across scientific fields and allow tools to be reused across distinct simulation environments. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2023/26}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-22.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Make scientific simulation environments interoperable.

